      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find $x$, if $5a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-5a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-5a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
